  "body": "**Built on #1202 (merged to main as 75ad984c)** - its dialect reader and section derivation are unified here; nothing of #1202 is duplicated. The two predicates are now one.\n\n## What changed\n\n**First: the workholding limit no longer fails open.** Two reviews found the dangerous direction: a mill-turn's on-centre Drill at 8000 rpm under a 2000 rpm chuck posted `G97 S8000 M03` (head 81e4cb01), and the same drill with no machine loaded, or a mill machine, posted through either lathe post (head b0434952). The rule now keys on the POST that runs, not on the operation's kind; the machine's kind only ever widens what is judged (a milling post on a lathe or mill-turn, below):\n\n- Section: `lathe_voice::voice_of` (#1202's one derivation, also its lathe door; its live-tool test `post::dialect::states_live_tool` is what `post::dump` writes `PARAM LiveTool` from - the stream is byte-identical, all goldens and recorded suites untouched).\n- Script: `post::dialect::work_voice(cps)` - the manifest `capabilities` mask read three ways (turning -> work spindle, milling only -> tool spindle, none -> undeclared). `dialect::speaks_turning` now reads it too, so both rules share one mask reader.\n\nThird review (head c08685ea): a mill-turn's facing op at 3000 rpm under a 2000 rpm chuck posted `S3000 M3` through `fanuc.cps` / `haas.cps` (main refused it). Fixed: on a lathe or mill-turn a work-spindle section is judged at its rpm whatever the post calls itself - chosen over a door that refuses turning kinds through a milling post, because judging adds a refusal only over the limit, while a door would change programs that post today with no limit stated.\n\n### Every cell: machine kind x post dialect x section (verdict with a limit stated)\n\nWork = a section `lathe_voice::voice_of` puts on the work spindle (turning kinds, on-centre Drill); Tool = a milling section (door-refused under a turning post); C = live tool (moves state C).\n\n| Machine | Post | Work | Tool | C |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| none | turning | judged (on-centre drill; turning kinds not creatable) | not judged - #1190 door refuses it | C rate (no machine: no C rate -> refused by name) |\n| none | milling | not judged (tool spindle) | not judged | not judged (engine refuses a live section through a mill post) |\n| none | undeclared | judged | judged (stricter, #1199) | C rate |\n| mill | turning | judged (on-centre drill) | not judged - door refuses | C rate |\n| mill | milling | not judged (tool spindle; turning kinds not creatable) | not judged | not judged (engine refuses) |\n| mill | undeclared | judged | judged (stricter) | C rate |\n| mill-turn | turning | judged | not judged - door refuses | C rate |\n| mill-turn | milling | **judged (this fix)** | not judged (tool spindle) | C rate |\n| mill-turn | undeclared | judged | judged (stricter) | C rate |\n| lathe | turning | judged | n/a (milling kinds not creatable) | C rate |\n| lathe | milling | judged | judged (one spindle holds the chuck) | C rate |\n| lathe | undeclared | judged | n/a | C rate |\n\nPinned: the Work/Tool columns by `lathe_workholding_mill_post::every_machine_dialect_and_section_cell_gives_its_verdict` (facing and mill Face through fanuc-lathe / fanuc / undeclared on none, mill, mill-turn, lathe) and `lathe_workholding_kinds::a_lathe_post_is_held_to_the_chuck_whatever_machine_is_mounted` (on-centre drill, none and mill); the C column on a mill-turn by `lathe_workholding_live` (other machines' C cells read from the code, not built).\n\nAnd the original #1174 fix holds: a 10000 rpm live cross drill under a 100 rpm chuck is not refused by the tool's rpm. Refusal text shows one decimal when whole rpm would print the speed and the limit the same (\"2000.4 rpm ... maximum of 2000.0 rpm\").\n\nNo post script touched. MCP `set_workholding_max_rpm` unchanged. Decision: `docs/decisions/1174-chuck-limit-work-spindle-only.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `lathe_workholding_mill_post::a_mill_turn_facing_op_through_a_milling_post_is_held_to_the_chuck` (fanuc and haas: 3000 over 2000 refused by name, at 2000 posts; fails on c08685ea)\n- `lathe_workholding_mill_post::a_mill_turn_milling_section_through_a_milling_post_is_not_judged` (mill Face at 8000 posts `S8000` through fanuc and haas)\n- `lathe_workholding_mill_post::every_machine_dialect_and_section_cell_gives_its_verdict`\n\n- `lathe_workholding_kinds::a_lathe_post_is_held_to_the_chuck_whatever_machine_is_mounted` (no machine and a mill machine, fanuc-lathe and tormach-lathe: refused at 8000, posts at exactly 2000)\n- `lathe_workholding_kinds::a_mill_post_drives_the_tool_spindle_so_the_chuck_limit_does_not_judge_it` (fanuc.cps posts `S8000 M3` with a limit stated)\n- `lathe_workholding_kinds::an_undeclared_script_takes_the_stricter_reading` (fanuc-lathe without its manifest line: refused)\n- `lathe_workholding_kinds::a_milling_script_on_a_plain_lathe_still_turns_the_work`\n- `lathe_workholding_kinds::a_speed_a_hair_over_the_chuck_prints_a_decimal`\n- `lathe_workholding_kinds::a_mill_turn_on_centre_drill_is_judged_like_the_lathes` (+ the Bore is refused by the #1202 door), the per-kind table tests (lathe, mill-turn in thirds, heavy slow-kinds lane)\n- `lathe_workholding_live` (cross drill not judged; C section by C rate; unrated C), `lathe_workholding_rpm` (G97 3000/2000 refused; G96 clamp; `None` posts as before)\n- `post::dialect::tests::the_mask_names_the_spindle_a_plain_section_drives`\n\n## How tested\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-post`: 223 passed, 0 failed. App: lathe_workholding_mill_post 3 (new), lathe_workholding_kinds 10 (+1 heavy), lathe_workholding_live 3, lathe_workholding_rpm 6, lathe_work_spindle 5, mcp_workholding 1, lathe_spindle_law 8, lathe_post 7, lathe_post_css 10, c_axis_live 5, c_axis_unwind 7, recorded_post_streams 2, operations 117, golden_cl 25, project_roundtrip 71 - all pass. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` green on the final head.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNot run on a real machine. Kinds that do not generate from seed params on the test bar are covered by the derivation, not posted one by one. The heavy slow-kinds row was not re-run after the #1202 merge. A posed or off-centre section under an undeclared script is judged at its rpm (stricter than needed, until #1199). C sections are judged by the stated C ceiling, not per-move C speed. `work_voice` loads the script in the JS engine; the gate caches it once per distinct post.\n\nChangelog: The workholding (chuck) rpm limit is judged for the post that runs: every section a turning post opens on the work spindle is held to it whatever the operation or machine (a mill-turn's on-centre drill, or a lathe post with no or a mill machine, is refused over the limit), C-axis live-tool sections by the machine's C rate, a milling post's tool spindle is not judged, and a live-tool cross drill is no longer refused by the tool's rpm\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1174\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
